  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0360\" is used to store information about system logs, operators, and operations. It contains three tables: \"Log\", \"Operator\", and \"Operation_Log\".\nThe \"Log\" table stores information about system logs, including the category, content, creation time, deletion time, ID, last modified time, and level. The ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are not nullable.\nThe \"Operator\" table stores information about operators, including the account, contact information, ID, and password. The ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are not nullable.\nThe \"Operation_Log\" table stores information about operations, including the execution content, log ID, operation time, operation type, and user ID. The primary key is a composite of the log ID, user ID, and operation time, and the foreign keys reference the \"Log\" and \"Operator\" tables. The update and delete rules for the foreign keys are set to CASCADE.",
  "gold_question": "The business requirements description for the log management system: The system is designed to record and manage operational logs, supporting the creation, modification, and deletion of logs. The system must capture detailed information for each log, including log level, content, category, and lifecycle (creation, modification, and deletion timestamps). Each log operation must be associated with an operator, who possesses an ID, account, password, contact information, permissions, and user role. By recording the relationship between logs and operators, the system can track the operational history of each log, including operation time, operation type, and execution content. Additionally, the system supports categorized management of logs to ensure the traceability and integrity of log data.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0360.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0360\nCREATE TABLE `Log` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `deletion_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_modified_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Operator` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Operation_Log` (\n  `log_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `execution_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`log_id`, `user_id`, `operation_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `operation_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`log_id`) REFERENCES `Log` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `operation_log_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `Operator` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
